{
  "_comment": [
    "Mechanical transcription of all 120 base-box Tag Team fight cards (12 fighters x 10).",
    "Source: the PUBLIC BGA card art listed in sources.json. Numbers and op lists only --",
    "no flavour text, no art. tools/import_bga.py reads this into fighters.py.",
    "",
    "A CARD is one entry. `copies` is how many physical copies sit in that fighter's deck,",
    "printed on the card as its frequency badge. `starting` marks the fighter's Starting Card;",
    "one of its copies carries the star and is set aside at setup, the rest live in the Build",
    "Deck. `art_ids` are BGA's image ids -- the star copy is drawn separately, which is why some",
    "cards list two.",
    "",
    "OPS. Each op is {op, ...}. `target` defaults to 'self' and is one of:",
    "  self | partner | opp | opp_partner | both_opps | all_others | all",
    "  attack          - target loses HP equal to the Active Fighter's Power at START of turn",
    "  block           - negate every Attack by opp and opp_partner. `success` fires if it",
    "                    negated at least one Attack, even a 0-Power one, at most once a turn",
    "  damage n        - Direct Damage. Not an Attack; unblockable; still stopped by 'stop'",
    "                    and still triggers health-track icons",
    "  heal n          - move the marker up. n may be a computed value (see below)",
    "  power n         - add (n>0) or remove (n<0) Power cubes",
    "  transfer_power  - {n, from, to}; move as much as you have, up to n",
    "  cancel          - the opposing fighter's card is ignored entirely",
    "  track           - {track, n} advance a fighter's own special track",
    "  if              - {cond, then, else}",
    "  fx              - {name} -> FIGHTER_FX[name]; anything not expressible declaratively",
    "",
    "`success` on an attack fires when it is NOT Blocked; on a block, when it negated >=1 Attack.",
    "`after: true` marks an op that must resolve AFTER the ops before it (the printed THEN keyword).",
    "A computed n is an object, e.g. {\"kind\": \"power\"} = as many as you have Power."
  ],

  "schema": 1,

  "known_gaps": [
    "Milady's 11 Intrigue (Scheme) tokens carry only 9 DISTINCT abilities, listed in",
    "milady_schemes below and taken verbatim-in-mechanics from BGA's own i18n strings.",
    "Which 2 are duplicated is not visible in any public source -- the art is a face-down",
    "pile. A gamedatas dump or a replay settles it; until then import_bga.py must not",
    "silently guess. See data/README.md.",
    "",
    "Ching Shih's 'Terror of the Seas' prints effects for 0-7, 8-15 and exactly 20 Ships.",
    "16-19 is deliberately blank on the card -- it does nothing but the trailing THEN +1 Ship."
  ],

  "milady_schemes": {
    "_comment": "9 distinct Intrigue effects across 11 tokens. Revealed tokens leave the game. From a CARD they resolve with that card; from the HEALTH TRACK they resolve after all card actions, which is how they can move a marker sitting on a stop. Poison always resolves LAST of all Intrigues, against the HP total after everything else.",
    "effects": [
      {"id": "attack_and_unleash", "ops": [{"op": "attack"}, {"op": "unleash_scheme"}]},
      {"id": "attack_both", "ops": [{"op": "attack", "target": "both_opps"}]},
      {"id": "partner_heal_6", "ops": [{"op": "heal", "n": 6, "target": "partner"}]},
      {"id": "all_take_1", "ops": [{"op": "damage", "n": 1, "target": "all"}]},
      {"id": "gain_2_power", "ops": [{"op": "power", "n": 2, "target": "self"}]},
      {"id": "partner_gains_2_power", "ops": [{"op": "power", "n": 2, "target": "partner"}]},
      {"id": "unleash_and_partner_power", "ops": [{"op": "unleash_scheme"}, {"op": "power", "n": 1, "target": "partner"}]},
      {"id": "both_gain_1_power", "ops": [{"op": "power", "n": 1, "target": "self"}, {"op": "power", "n": 1, "target": "partner"}]},
      {"id": "poison", "ops": [{"op": "fx", "name": "milady_poison"}],
       "_comment": "Direct Damage equal to half the Opponent's CURRENT HP, rounded down, so it can never KO. Resolves after every other Intrigue."}
    ],
    "total_tokens": 11
  },

